<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman annexation of Syria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">63 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> took place in 63 BCE, when the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> deposed the last Seleucid rulers and organised Syria as a Roman province. By then the Seleucid state had been reduced to a small, divided remnant around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>. The event marked the formal end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>, which had once stretched from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p></div>
